{
  "dom_id": "step-q61858",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Owen enrolled in an online course that has $12$ topics. He completed $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the remaining topics every week. Which expression gives approximately  the number of topics that were incomplete after $3$ weeks?",
  "worked_solution": "If the number of incomplete topics decreased by $\\frac{1}{6}$ every week, then every week $\\frac{5}{6}$ of the topics remained incomplete.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ week, $12\\cdot (\\frac{5}{6})$ topics were incomplete.\n\n- After $2$ weeks, approximately  $12\\cdot {(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}$ topics were incomplete.\n\n- After $3$ weeks, approximately $12\\cdot {(\\frac{5}{6})}^{3}$ topics were incomplete.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
